 CONCLUSION:
   sup CV(N_R)^2 in scan = 8.736 (dense R + speed 7); it GROWS as m_R->0,
   so the clean gatekeeper CV^2 < m_Q/(1-m_Q) is NOT uniformly satisfied -- it FAILS for
   dense R even at the size-valid pairing. BUT actual R' stays > 0 throughout the scan:
   floor holds = True.  => the floor is TRUE on these cases but the clean
   CV gatekeeper alone does NOT prove it for dense R; the binding worst-case is the
   maximally-dense R with speed 7 (the 2-adic/7-adic resonance). The uniform proof must
   either restrict to the actual covering family or supplement the gatekeeper with the
   exact SPEC on dense R (where m_R->0 inflates the second moment).
